sentences.text:
The contents of the FIR as well as the statement under S.164 of CrPC leave no manner of doubt that, on the basis of the allegations as they stand, three important features emerge:
(i) The relationship between the appellant and the second respondent was on consensual nature;
(ii) The parties were in the relationship for about a period of one and a half years; and (iii) Subsequently, the appellant had expressed a disinclination to marry the second respondent which led to the registration of the FIR.
